+    <section class="journal" aria-labelledby="journal-title">
+      <h2 id="journal-title">Roaster's Journal</h2>
+      <div class="journal-text" id="journal-text">
+        <p>Every bag we roast begins months before it reaches our shop, usually at a long wooden table in a
+          farmer's courtyard, where we taste dozens of small lots side by side. We buy from cooperatives and
+          family farms in Colombia, Ethiopia, Guatemala, and Sumatra, and we return to the same producers year
+          after year so that both sides can plan, invest, and improve together.</p>
+        <p>We pay well above the Fair Trade minimum, and we agree on the price before the harvest rather than after
+          it. That gives growers the security to hire pickers at fair wages, repair their wet mills, and
+          experiment with processing methods like honey and anaerobic fermentation. When a lot cups especially
+          well, we pay a quality premium directly to the farm, with no broker in the middle.</p>
+        <p>Once green coffee lands at the port, we cup every arriving sample again against the pre-shipment
+          sample. If it does not match, it does not go into a bag. We then run small test roasts, adjusting
+          temperature and time until the profile highlights what makes that lot special, whether that is the
+          jasmine and bergamot of a washed Ethiopian or the cocoa and brown sugar of a Guatemalan Huehuetenango.</p>
+        <p>Sourcing is also seasonal. Our menu changes with the harvest because fresh crop coffee tastes better,
+          and we would rather sell out of a favorite than serve a tired bean. We share the farm, the altitude, and
+          the harvest date on every bag, so you know exactly where your cup came from and who grew it.</p>
+      </div>
+      <button type="button" class="btn summarize-btn" id="summarize-btn">Summarize</button>
+      <p class="summary-status" id="summary-status" role="status"></p>
+      <div class="summary-output" id="summary-output" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
+    </section>
